{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/535107-facilities","id":535107,"title":"Facilities","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-05-31T19:52:17-07:00","id":535107,"title":"Facilities","content":"I don't see these discussed very often, and compared to Infrastructure they get very little page count.<br /> <br /> Which is odd, since you'd think Matrix meets Silent Hill would have all sorts of potential.<br /> <br /> Has anyone used these in a Chronicle (including a non DtD)? Does anyone have any to share?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2233-agentwestmer","name":"Agentwestmer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2233_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-01T08:45:06-07:00","id":535646,"title":"","content":"To me, a facility is just another form of Infrastructure. Everything that the God-Machine does is build Infrastructure. Make an angel factory? You're just making more stuff in order to build a better mouse trap. A facility that spies on people, then decides their fate, and then their will executed in the form of a giant news room? Same. A brainwashing facility to create sleeper agents? Most anything that Deva Corp produces? Pretty much the vast majority of Command and Control Infrastructure? <br /> <br /> The God-Machine is constantly building new facilities in order to create more material for even more advanced Infrastructure projects, so you can have more advanced facilities, for even more advanced projects, and so on. They're so wrapped up together that, as far as I'm personally concerned, there's no difference between them. At best, I would label a facility as a place where long term projects are carried out, or long term production/storage/etc of something the God-Machine wants for its Infrastructures. Still a part, its just long term use Infrastructure instead of one use then scrub Infrastructure. <br /> <br /> So, yes. I have a setting where the Tempters have a suborned facility as a base - much like Seattle, it involved time manipulation, so they used it to form a time bubble, living in an alternate &quot;Tomorrowland&quot; universe where no people naturally existed. The facility not only processes Essence to run the time bubble, but provides a wealth of aether for visiting demons, and has enough protection and cultists that demons feel safe relaxing without fear of angels.<br /> <br /> <br /> My local Command and Control center is hidden from reality in a parallel time stream again, though this one is more like a rip off of Heaven. Pearly (computer) gateways to enter, golden roads (look like circuitry), music from the vast forges that resonate along the four Influences in a harmonius whole. This is staffed entirely by angels and highly modified android-like humans to resemble angels. That counts as well, I imagine. &quot;Everytime a bell rings, an angel gets its wings.&quot; Which is true, in a way, because this facility stores, recovers, reconfigures, and makes angels, and a bell like sound accompanies each final process. As well, lots of information is used to determine the course of the local city's inhabitants.<br /> <br /> A secondary facility is assigned for &quot;blessing&quot; cultists and cryptids, or making Sleeper agents. <br /> <br /> There's a number of cultist worship-spaces where they make sacrifices. I call these facilities &quot;power plants&quot; because they provide the sacrifices necessary to produce essence, which flows through the city's Infrastructure to power every angel and every other Infrastructure out there.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-01T13:03:10-07:00","id":535865,"title":"","content":"I used a pair of GM Facilities in the werewolf game I was running for a short story. The first was a harvesting facility embedded in the local community center. After every convention held there, a cultist would summon several spirits at the basement, and basically tell them, &quot;look, your well of essence for this year is gone. why not slumber in this handy fetter, and I'll wake you up when your convention comes back.&quot; The spirits that agreed to be bound were sliced apart by the infrastructure, and their traits (influences, numina, attributes, etc) were bound up in separate occult canisters. This process required human sacrifices in a separate room (hidden by spatial folding) to complete.<br /> <br /> The canisters would then be transported to The Clocktower, which was the city's broadcasting facility. It was basically an abandoned building, whose owner was paid handsomely to keep the power on and everyone out. Homeless people often crashed there, and got defensive about it - a guardian angel masqueraded as one. It connected to &quot;maintenance tunnels&quot;, full of cryptids, where the infrastructure was housed. The canisters of shredded spirit traits were brought here to be digitally transmitted to the angel building / storage facility at NORAD [which wasn't seen in game].<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> For a while, the GM was using a human cultist to do the sacrifices and transfer the occult canisters. He was given an artifact with a spatial un-folding spell in order to get in. He then met up with a car spirit which could abduct him into Twilight on his way to the Clocktower (which allowed him to bypass the cryptid guards and access the infrastructure controls). The whole thing really took a toll on his mind; he went a little ax-crazy, a liability to the plans, and eventually died in the tunnels. Since then, an angel carried on his work.<br /> <br /> My pack of werewolves was alerted to this by a helping a homeless friend of theirs investigate his missing girlfriend (the sacrifices were usually the homeless or prostitutes - easier targets). They tracked the dead cultist into the maintenance tunnels to retrieve the artifact, use it to break into the sacrificial room, battled angels and dropped some C4 to wreck the place. Then they called some Bone Shadow allies to let them know about some strange not-spirit / not-ghost ephemeral people they fought, and suggested they get on hunting them to figure out how they work.<br /> <br /> I was intending a followup, where the community center would start &quot;repairing&quot; the damage they did as a lure to set a hunter-killer angel on them. The GM would meanwhile build its new harvesting facility at the local university. However, I didn't get around to telling that story before the chronicle petered out.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> It was a fun little diversion which got the pack well out of their element. Since I was adapting it to a werewolf game, I limited my presentation to problems that they would care about and be able to solve, which kind of detoured it away from the main themes of God Machine and DtD, but it was a nice way of demonstrating the overlapping <i>high strangeness </i>of the setting in a way the players decided they definitely didn't want to get involved in again.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Second Chance for<br /> <img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=709\" data-tempid=\"temp_709_1572548741915_354\" /><br /> A Beautiful Madness</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/425-seraph-kitty","name":"Seraph Kitty","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar425_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}